## 12. THREE-DAY REVIEW JOURNEY

The summative test is imminent, so include a recommended three-day learning path.

**Day 1 — Discover and Diagnose**

- Short diagnostic.
- Foundation lessons.
- Focus on increasing and decreasing number patterns.
- Introduce letters and repeating patterns.
- Identify weak areas.

**Day 2 — Practice and Build**

- Review weak competencies.
- Practice visual and rhythmic patterns.
- Emphasize creating original increasing and decreasing patterns.
- Mixed practice.
- Revisit previously missed questions.

**Day 3 — Prove Your Powers**

- Brief warm-up.
- Full mixed-topic mock assessment.
- Review incorrect answers.
- Short targeted reinforcement session.
- Optional confidence-building challenge.

Each daily mission should fit into approximately 15 minutes where practical, while allowing the child to return for additional sessions.

Make the journey flexible. A parent must be able to access any day or mode without waiting for real-world calendar time.

